# Files Semgrep should NOT scan. Same syntax as .gitignore.
# Goal: skip generated code, build artefacts, vendored dependencies,
# and noisy test fixtures so signal stays high.

# --- Build outputs ---
**/dist/
**/build/
**/.next/
**/out/
**/coverage/

# --- Vendored / installed deps ---
**/node_modules/
**/vendor/
**/.pnpm-store/
backend/test-results/
test-results/

# --- Mobile (Flutter) build artefacts ---
mobile/.dart_tool/
mobile/build/
mobile/ios/Pods/
mobile/android/.gradle/
mobile/android/build/
mobile/android/app/build/

# --- Generated / minified ---
*.min.js
*.min.css
*.bundle.js
*.map

# --- Lockfiles (separate concern; covered by dependency scanners) ---
package-lock.json
yarn.lock
pnpm-lock.yaml
mobile/pubspec.lock

# --- Test fixtures we DON'T want flagged for hardcoded test creds ---
**/*.spec.ts
**/*.test.ts
tests/
backend/test/

# --- DB dumps / large generated SQL ---
*.sql.gz
masterdata_backup.sql

# --- Documentation ---
docs/
planning/

# --- Worktrees: avoid double-scanning the same code ---
.claude/worktrees/

# --- Skip our own audit log fields if they ever land in code (false positives) ---
# (none right now; placeholder for future)
